WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.675
The pages aren't six separate
lists; they build on each other.

2
00:00:03.675 --> 00:00:06.865
The Federal Framework
Crosswalk is the wide view,

3
00:00:06.865 --> 00:00:09.200
every book against every framework.

4
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.614
The RMF Map takes its Risk Management
Framework row and goes task by task; where

5
00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:19.862
the two disagree, the map wins, and the
crosswalk's RMF score is derived from it.

6
00:00:19.862 --> 00:00:25.638
The M-19-17 and FICAM Crosswalk does
the same deep dive for identity policy.

7
00:00:25.638 --> 00:00:30.466
The Microsoft Practice Crosswalk shows the
specific practices behind the evidence,

8
00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:32.234
each tied to an automated check,

9
00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:36.587
and the Command Reference lists the kit
commands that produce that evidence.

10
00:00:36.587 --> 00:00:40.638
Underneath all of them sits the
Source Register, so every source the

11
00:00:40.638 --> 00:00:45.120
slides and videos cite has a permanent
address that is checked every week.
